															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weryllium" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2727655); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2727655&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607570741" alt="Weryllium" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2727655)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/weryllium" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2727655); return false;" >Weryllium</a></span> <span class="odate time_1547076807 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">09 Jan 2019 23:33</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4114124">
									

<p>Came to me at 3 am last night. <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/9volt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2800867&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1547077218" alt="9Volt" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2800867)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/9volt" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2800867); return false;">9Volt</a></span> and <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2198340&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1547077218" alt="Kakroom" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2198340)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/kakroom" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2198340); return false;">Kakroom</a></span> said it didn't suck.</p>
<p>Pic is from <a href="https://commons.m.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sledgehammer_(33104910115).jpg">https://commons.m.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sledgehammer_(33104910115).jpg</a> CC 2.0 generic.</p>
<p>On the off chance that whoever left a draft in here is still around and still wants it, I've copied it below.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">blah</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Item# : SCP 6969</p>
<p>Object Class: Euclid</p>
<p>Special Containment Procedures: Item must be kept in a 3x3x3 meter room, the room must be lined with high quality sound muffling material. The room must be installed with an air-lock system. The room must be vacumed when not in use.</p>
<p>In fear of witnessing &quot;The Smile&quot; of the object, Video recording or surveillance of the item’s screen is strictly prohibited, any unauthorized personnel attempts to do so, will be detained and remove from the site forcefully.</p>
<p>Recording of the sound must be done by two authorized personnel in a sound proof room, one of the personnel shall write any data that is deemed useful on an A4 sized lined paper. Conversations with the item or sayings from the test subject(s) shall be written in script format. The scientific personnel need to wear ear mufflers and watch over the D-Class personnel. If the D-Class are acting irregularly then the personnel must turn off the recording and take the D-Class for a full mental survey.</p>
<p>Listening to the item's song for more than 10 minutes is not recommended. In addition, test subjects that has been with the item for more than 25 minutes with the item must be killed as they become SCP-6969-02</p>
<p>In case of containment breach of SCP- 6969-02 with SCP-6969, combat personel must first wear ear mufflers before engaging and eradicating SCP 6969-02. After eradicating SCP-6969-02, cover SCP- 6969 with an opaque fabric then carry it on to SCP-6969, bring it back to it's cell and place it back on the table, then call in a D class personnel to set it up right on the phone stand provided before removing the cloak.</p>
<p>Description: SCP-6969 is an Apple branded touch screen phone playing looped video of a person of an unspecified gender due to the person portraying as both female and male dancing to a song starting off with the words &quot;Hit or Miss&quot; (see Addendum SCP 6969-B). However, it has been confirmed by one of the test subject (see Addendum<br />
SCP 6969-B) that the person is wearing a female cheerleader attire.</p>
<p>When listening to SCP-6969 song, reports have shown that the victim experiences the following symptoms: Absent-Mindedness, fatigued or irregular muscle spasms.When watching SCP-6969 looped video, victims describe that they feel relaxed and awestruck. After an extended period of time spent with SCP-6969, victim will not respond to any vocal or audible stimuli, when attempt to make physical contact victim will retaliate,<br />
at this point the victim can now be confirmed as SCP-6969-02</p>
<p>SCP-6969 was found on ██/█/2018 at █████ street in California, ██████ when Agent █████, which was off duty at the time, and is now dead, found a group of people staring at an iPhone (SCP- 6969).<br />
Agent █████ was killed due to him becoming SCP 6969-02, Agent █████ brought SCP 6969 to the site, laughing and having spasms, he was under the influence of SCP 6969.</p>
<p>Addendum SCP 6969-B:</p>
<p>Transcript between Dr.█████ and D-1783:</p>
<p>Dr.█████: D-1783, explain what exactly you see?<br />
D-1783: It's, an iPhone? An iPhone X.<br />
Dr.█████: Alright<br />
D-1783: I feel&#8230;so [Incoherent mumbling]<br />
Dr.█████: Can you please repeat?<br />
[ No response from D-1783]<br />
Dr.█████: Are you there, D-1783?<br />
[ No respons from D-1783]<br />
Dr.█████: Answer me D-1783 or we will have to send a security guard to terminate you.<br />
D-1783: That&#8230;&#8230;<br />
Dr.█████: What are you seeing?<br />
D-1783: That&#8230;. smile&#8230;. its perfect<br />
Dr.█████: Can you describe what you are seeing, D-1783?<br />
Unclear audio, song can be made out to be iLOVEFRiDAY - Mia Khalifa.<br />
Dr.█████: Hello?<br />
D-1783: I guess they never miss.. [followed by mumbling)<br />
[End Transmission]</p>
<p>Officer █████ and Officer █████ (both KIA) were sent in to retrieve D-1783, When Officer █████ tried to grab D-1783, D-1783 retaliate by throwing himself onto Officer █████ and punching him in the head multiple times, causing bleeding and breaking of the skull. Officer █████ died from the breakage of his skull on the spot.. D-1783 rushed towards Officer █████, D-1783 was shot in the head.</p>
